  "notes": "Official 'The BSN Program Four Year Academic Schedule' from the NPU Prelicensure Baccalaureate Student Handbook AY 23-24 (the most recent prelicensure handbook verifiable on northpark.edu; labeled honestly). The handbook states course selections should be made with advisor consent. Transcription notes: (1) Semester credit sums from the printed courses are 16/16/16/17/13/16/15/12 = 121; the handbook's own printed year totals (32/32/31/25-27) do not all reconcile with its course rows (2nd-year rows sum to 33 not 32; 3rd-year rows sum to 29 not 31) — courses transcribed exactly as printed. (2) 'Optional - NURS 3920 Cardiac Dysrhythmias (2)' is marked optional in the source and is excluded from the term plan; documented here. (3) NURS 4901 Nursing Comprehensive Exam is 0 credits, P/F — modeled as required_zero. (4) '*' in the source marks prerequisite courses for the nursing major (admission block): BIOL 1250, BIOL 1260, CHEM 1021, CHEM 1031, BIOL 2910, BIOL 2930, NURS 3240, PSYC 1000, PSYC 2700, SOC 1910, HSC 1490, CORE 1000, NURS 2100, and NURS 2540 or EXS 3180 — all must be completed with a grade of C or better (C- not acceptable) plus cumulative GPA 2.75 and separate science GPA 2.75, TEAS 'Proficient', and at most two prerequisite repeats (only one science). Students must have 120 hours to graduate; the last 30 hours must be taken at NPU; no credit may transfer after 90 credits. '+' marks Core Curriculum requirements.",
